<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.11.1: Relating a Quadratic Function and Its Zeros</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02272</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.11.1: Relating a Quadratic Function and Its Zeros</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bd6b7da9-34fa-4e45-87b3-555b9d2b5417</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Write the quadratic function \(f(x) = x^2 − 9x + 20\) in factored form.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Enter the quadratic function in factored form.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00004">\(f(x) = (x − 4)(x − 5)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">What are the solutions of the quadratic equation \((x − 4)(x − 5) = 0\)?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">Enter the solutions of the quadratic equation.</para>
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00008">\(x = 4\) and \(x = 5\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Graph the quadratic function \(f(x) = x^2− 9x + 20\).</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00009">Use the Desmos graphing tool or technology outside the course.</para>
      <media alt="...">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Enter the \(x\)-intercepts.</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00013">\((4, 0)\), \((5, 0)\) or 4 and 5</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00014">Marcus states that the zeros of the function of \(f(x) = x^2 − 9x + 20\) are 4 and 5. Do you agree? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00015">Enter your answer and your reasoning.</para>
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00017">Yes, 4 and 5 are the input values that result in an output of 0. When the function \(f(x) = x^2 − 9x + 20\) is graphed, it crosses the \(x\)-axis at \(x=4\) and \(x=5\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
